    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0095" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.24/951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Asmara</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Asmara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-01T10:00:00+03:00">February 1,
                            1943—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:57 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>13. General Maxwell<anchor n="6" xml:id="d99-f1"/> and Colonel Clark Commanding
                    Officer Asmara will be at Addis Ababa February 9. Colonel Clark suggests <pb
                        facs="0096" n="84" xml:id="pg84"/> I go up with him to report to the
                    Department probable inquiries on lease-lend by Emperor. Shall I proceed?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d99-f1" n="6" xml:id="d99-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. R. L. Maxwell, Commanding General, Services of Supply, U. S. Army
                    Forces in the Middle East</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
